  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#InsuranceContract">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Insurance Contract Under Consideration</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A life insurance agreement under consideration for issuance or review. Induced from a Hierarchy placement via graph-native parent (entity role co-occurrence): subClassOf POLICY; cluster of 1 surface variant(s) merged in…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Invalid provisions do not affect remaining policy validity. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The clause ensures legal resilience of remaining terms, aligning with 'LegalFramework' as the domain of enforceabilit…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy lapses if premiums are not paid within a period. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property defines a time-based lapse condition tied to nonpayment, with 'Period' as the appropriate range. Evidence co…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Adjusts death benefit for misstated sex. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The policy-level adjustment for misstated sex directly affects the death benefit amount. The property 'deathBenefitAmountSpecification'…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy incontestable after two years. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The incontestability period is defined as a two-year duration from issue, making it a temporal condition. The property 'hasIncontestability…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Coverage during grace period. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The grace period is a defined time interval during which coverage remains in force. The property 'hasGracePeriod' directly links the contract to th…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Deduction applied for unpaid premiums from death benefit. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that unpaid premiums are deducted from the death benefit, and the range is PaymentAmount as it re…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Suicide exclusion restarts after policy reinstatement. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The sentences confirm that the suicide exclusion applies anew from the reinstatement date, indicating a resumption of the…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy void from inception due to age misstatement. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states that misstated age leads to void ab initio, meaning the policy is invalid from the start. The property is…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy remains valid after contestability period ends. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property is tied to the duration of the contestability period, and the evidence confirms that validity extends beyond…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Excludes participation in company earnings. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The policy feature explicitly excludes surplus and earnings sharing, and NonParticipatingPolicy is the correct class to represent thi…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Prevents future dividend payments under certain conditions. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The property expresses a binary condition (dividends payable or not), and the evidence confirms future dividends are…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A life insurance agreement under consideration for issuance or review.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#ContractualProvision"/>
